om the occupied list:\n- H13: X ✅\n- I13: X ✅\n- J13: X ✅\n- K13: X ✅\n- L13: X ✅\n\nYes! That’s **five connected black stones** on row 13.\n\nBut the current turn is **Black to move** — which means the last move must have been White. If Black already had five in a row, the game should have ended. But since it\'s still going and we\'re being asked to move, this suggests one possibility: **did Black just complete this five-in-a-row on their previous move and the game didn’t end? Or is this an oversight?**\n\nBut wait — let’s double-check the list of occupied coordinates:\n\nFrom input:\n> H13, I13, J13, K13, L13\n\nAnd the symbol key:\n- X = Black\n- O = White\n\nIn the board layout:\nRow 13: `|13|.|.|.|.|.|.|.|X|X|O|X|X|.|.|.|` ← Wait! This contradicts!\n\nHold on — in the text board:\n\n|13|.|.|.|.|.|.|.|X|X|O|X|X|.|.|.|  \n\nSo:\n- H13: X\n- I13: X\n- J13: O ← This is White!\n- K13: X\n- L13: X\n\nAh! Critical correction: **J13 is O (White)**, not X.\n\nBut in the "Occupied Coordinates" list, it says:  \n"J13" — but doesn\'t specify color. However, earlier it lists:  \n"J2, C3, I3, D4, H4, E5, H5, M5, F6, G6, H6, I6, L6, G7, H7, I7, J7, K7, F8, H8, I8, J8, K8, G9, H9, I9, H10, I10, J10, G11, H11, I11, J11, K11, L11, I12, J12, H13, I13, J13, K13, L13, H14, K14"\n\nBut from the board rendering:\n- J13: O (White) — because in row 13: `... |X|X|O|X|X| ...` at H13, I13, J13, K13, L13\n\nSo J13 is White.\n\nThus, the sequence on row 13 is: H13(X), I13(X), J13(O), K13(X), L13(X) — **not connected**.\n\nBack to analysis.\n\nLet’s look for **potential four-in-a-row or open threes**.\n\nFocus on **row 7**:  \nG7(X), H7(X), I7(O), J7(X), K7(X)\n\nNot useful.\n\nRow 8: F8(O), H8(X), I8(X), J8(O), K8(O)\n\nNo.\n\nRow 11: G11(O), H11(X), I11(X), J11(X), K11(X), L11(O)\n\nSo H11, I11, J11, K11 — **four black stones in a row**, between G11(O) and L11(O) — **fully blocked**. No way to extend.\n\nNow, **diagonal from G7 to K11**:  \nG7(X), H8(X), I9(X), J10(O), K11(X) — broken.\n\n